fact WorkItem(id: "WI-419", description: some(value: "entries_cover Strategy-1 requirement forwarding ignores same-unified-variable identity (LATENT, pre-existing; surfaced by WI-418 /code-review). build_dep_projection Strategy 1 (typing.rs ~4258) matches a callee requirement dep against a caller `requires` entry via entries_cover (~4296), then emits `var_ref(__req_<name>)` that forwards the caller's requirement to the callee at eval. entries_cover keys ONLY on (required_sort + per-binding compat) and ACCEPTS when either side is a type-param wildcard (is_type_param_value, ~4327-4329); it does NOT check that the dep's element is the SAME unified logical variable as the caller binding's element. HAZARD: a caller (sort/op) declaring TWO `requires` of the SAME spec sort over DISTINCT element params (e.g. `requires Eq[A], Eq[B]` with A != B) + an ABSTRACT cross-sort callee dep over (say) B: Strategy 1 `position`-matches the FIRST same-spec caller entry (Eq[A]) and forwards `__req` for A — the WRONG dictionary — instead of B's. Eval would then dispatch the callee's deferred spec op through the wrong impl. PRE-EXISTING: entries_cover/Strategy 1 are the live path for same-sort + WI-415 + WI-418; WI-418 only routes MORE abstract cross-sort calls through it. SOUND for every shape currently exercised (each spec sort has a SINGLE covering requirement), so no known code triggers it and no test fails today — this is defensive/correctness-hardening, likely hard to repro without a contrived 2-same-spec-requires sort. FIX DIRECTION: when both sides are type-param wildcards, disambiguate by the element's unification identity — verify the dep's element var resolves (via the call-site subst) to the SAME var as the caller binding's element, rather than accepting any same-spec entry; or thread enough call-site context into build_dep_projection to pick the correct slot when multiple same-spec requires exist. ACCEPTANCE: a 2-same-spec-requires repro (caller requires Eq[A],Eq[B]; cross-sort abstract call needing Eq on B) forwards B's __req not A's; suite green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-06-17T16:56:09Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-419", author: "user", content: "Type-side twin filed 2026-06-10: WI-428 (RigidTypeProjection) stores the full CANONICAL bound application (not the bare spec symbol) precisely so two same-spec requires over distinct bindings stay distinct TYPE identities -- the projection-identity counterpart of this dict-forwarding ambiguity. WI-430 promotes the carrier-precision fix for the delivered ExprCarried neutral path. A fix here should keep the disambiguation rule aligned with theirs (identity = canonical application + member, carrier var by sigma-class).", at: "2026-06-10T20:38:32Z")
